                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 3,
                "source": "Twitter Web Client",
                "text": "From the start of Year 1, we were clear: Behavioral health and successful reentry are priorities at the highest level of state government.\n\nWe created a Recovery and Reentry Commissioner \u2013 the first Cabinet position of its kind in the country \u2013 to bring focus, coordination and accountability to work that touches public safety, workforce and families across North Dakota.\n\nWorking with the Legislature, we directed over $30 million to add dozens of behavioral health beds in Bismarck, Grand Forks and Williston, including beds for youths in need of behavioral health services.\n\nAnd the state continued to strengthen reentry supports and ensure people leaving incarceration have real pathways to stability, employment and long-term success.\n\nWhen government treats behavioral health as a core responsibility, not an afterthought, communities are safer and stronger.",
